{
  "//": "Feature 32, the wandering shaman (plan Documentation/Design/Harsh_Wilds_Content_Update_As_Built.md section 32, Open question 22, W0-20 in Wave 0 findings). The FIRST Harsh Wilds NPCAgent. A data-only visiting trader on the vanilla Agent_TraderGeneral chassis: born in Env_SpiritWorld at boot, registered by the minimal Agent.Ref manifest Animals/Shaman.json (the Owl's shape), moved on-stage and off by his own season-counter AgentActions. No CMC chassis code (W0-20 MEASURED). He is content the player meets by choice, so he has NO [Threats] switch (plan Open question 18).",
  "//trade": "CannotTrade false makes him a trader (InGameNPC.CanTrade is !CannotTrade && (TradingConditions.IsEmpty || valid); TradingConditions is a GeneralCondition struct, omitted = empty = always tradeable). His wares come the vanilla trader's way: each season's stock action, in the Spirit World eight ticks before he arrives, first clears his inventory (InventoryActions Type 0, ClearInventory, which InGameNPC runs BEFORE the action's drops) and then drops his wares into it (DropCardsInsideInventory). Wares are vanilla and Harsh Wilds items only: dried spirit mushrooms, dried fairyweed, dried fly agaric, the three spirit charms and winter mistletoe. TradingModifiers marks what he sells up by 1.5 (NPCToPlayer, Multiply). MaxCarryWeight 100000 as the vanilla trader. Every quantity and the markup are TUNABLE PLACEHOLDERS.",
  "//visit": "About once a season, one day (Open question 22, tunable). Per season four AgentActions on that season's vanilla SeasonCounter_* (0..2880, 96 ticks a day): stock at 760, arrive at the Green Glade (the vanilla trader's meeting place, Env_ClearingOak_GreenGlade b791dfa6...) at 768, an arrive retry at 784 (vanilla's trader retries its arrival too), depart to Env_SpiritWorld at 864, one day after arriving. Day 8 of the season keeps clear of the vanilla trader's own Green Glade stay (1440..2112, days 15 to 22 of spring and autumn). RepeatOptions 2 (ResetWhenConditionsAreFalse) re-arms each window once it has passed. Every window is a tunable placeholder.",
